# Radio > details on a Tern node: its firmware from the project's feed, installed over the link.
#
# One press, whichever bus or network the link is on, under a sheet of its own: the node keeps
# everything it holds and stays on the mesh while it takes the image, and a dropped link picks
# up where it stopped. There is no release list to choose - the feed is one line - and the
# screen's hint is the link's, not a bus's.
scene demo
clock 2026-10-14 14:20
delay 1800
config
protocol tern 9

tab radio
key down 9
key up
key a

# Firmware, Hardware, what the check found, the check, and the press under them.
firmware-install idle link
key down 4
hold 2000

key a
hold 3000
key b
hold 900

firmware-install downloading link 62
hold 1600
firmware-install arming link
hold 1200
firmware-install writing link 43
hold 1600
firmware-install waiting link
hold 1600
firmware-install writing link 81
hold 1200
firmware-install restarting link
hold 1400
firmware-install done link
hold 2400
key b
hold 900

firmware-install resolving link
firmware-install failed link
hold 2400
